# Valgrind memcheck suppressions for ct-ctgrind — reviewed, not blanket.
#
# Each entry below has been traced to a specific non-leak and is scoped
# as narrowly as Valgrind frame-matching allows. Fat LTO inlines most of
# the crypto path (the private op, the exponent ladder, unblinding) into
# the sign fixture at both opt-levels, so no entry may match on the
# fixture frame alone: each one names the routine it covers as the
# innermost frame. A secret-dependent branch anywhere else in the
# fixture, inlined or not, is reported.
#
# The one value that is public by design but computed from the secret,
# the verify-after-sign outcome, is declassified in the library through
# `ct_probe::declassify` (feature `ct-declassify`), not suppressed here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# (1) memcpy / memmove of tainted bytes.
#
# The fixture parses the secret exponent from bytes and shuffles
# secret-derived bytes through padding/serialization, calling
# memcpy/memmove on tainted memory. glibc's memcpy is *data-oblivious*
# (it copies bytes regardless of value), but Valgrind's shadow-value
# propagation through its word-at-a-time SIMD paths is imprecise and
# reports spurious errors *inside* the memcpy routine. Safe to suppress:
# memcpy never branches on the data it copies. A secret-dependent
# *address* would appear in the caller's address computation, a frame
# above — not matched here. Scoped to the sign fixture as the direct
# caller; with the crypto path inlined that covers its copies too,
# which is safe for the same reason: the copy never branches on the
# bytes.
{
   memcpy-tainted-data-from-sign-fixture-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*memcpy*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}
{
   memcpy-tainted-data-from-sign-fixture-value
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:*memcpy*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}
{
   memmove-tainted-data-from-sign-fixture-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*memmove*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}
{
   memmove-tainted-data-from-sign-fixture-value
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:*memmove*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# (2) Serialization of the PUBLIC RSA signature.
#
# The sign path serializes the signature with `i2osp_zeroizing_into`,
# which copies the carrier's full-width bytes into the modulus width and
# branches once on whether any byte above that width is non-zero
# (`try_be_pad_into`). For a valid signature (`s < n`) those bytes are
# always zero. The RSA signature is secret-*derived* but public-by-design
# (it is what the caller publishes), so this branch leaks nothing. Taint
# can't see through the "now public" declassification because we can't
# untaint mid-operation without instrumenting the sign.
#
# The entries cover Cond and Value8 when `try_be_pad_into` is a shared
# symbol called from a fixture. When it is inlined into the fixture the
# branch is not suppressed; if a build ever reports it there, give it its
# own declassification rather than matching the fixture frame.
{
   sig-serialize-try_be_pad_into-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*try_be_pad_into*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}
{
   sig-serialize-try_be_pad_into-value
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:*try_be_pad_into*
   fun:ct_fix__pkcs1v15_blinded_sign*
}
